  "topicId": "623156f3ac1bbd3914176d79",
  "name": "Lesson 1: Predict what you will hear",
  "slug": "lesson-1-predict-what-you-will-hear",
  "part": "part_1_photos",
  "descriptionHtml": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"background-color: #bfedd2;\"><strong style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 14pt; background-color: #bfedd2;\">1. Question type&nbsp;</strong></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 14pt;\">In this part, you are asked to see a picture and choose the statement that most describes the picture. To be able to choose the correct answer, you should think of the topic of the picture and possible statements.</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 14pt; background-color: #bfedd2;\"><strong>2. Guide to answer</strong></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 14pt;\">- Before the beginning of the section, think of the theme of the picture as well as brainstorm nouns and verbs related to the picture. You should do this because most distractors in the TOEIC part 1 involve the wrong noun or verb.</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 14pt;\">- Before listening, you also should predict possible statements. Most statements are about:</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 14pt;\">+ The activity</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>E.g.</strong> The man is writing an email.</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 14pt;\">+ The general situation</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>E.g.</strong> The meal is ready.</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 14pt;\">+ Spatial relationships&nbsp;</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>E.g.</strong> next to, near, across from, etc.)</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 14pt;\">- Focus while listening and choose the correct statement.&nbsp;</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\n"
}